PKG=zrtg46
NAME=z3660rtg-k46 1.1.2-2 - Z3660 and MNT ZZ9000 RTG graphics module, k46 line
ARCH=Amiga
VERSION=1.1.2-2
CATEGORY=system
CLASSES=none z3660rtg
VENDOR=amix
PSTAMP=amix-zrtg46-1.1.2-2
# Kernel space (amix-dlm C2-2, C3-5 v4 sec 1): a role=module entry of the
# #ext kpkg block (line=k46, kabi=k46.1.2), never an ordinary entry.  Catalog
# name z3660rtg-k46, pkginst zrtg46; VERSION is the module's 1.1.2-2 (the
# fork's module/VERSION at kernel/drivers/z3660rtg/z3660rtg.pin), its object
# built with the gcc-2.7.2.3-33ebadc kit, rolled from amix.  depend=monsw:
# composable only beside monsw46.  Major c 49 is 1.1's, so no APKG_KBOOTSET.
APKG_DESC=Z3660 and MNT ZZ9000 RTG graphics (the Z3660's onboard RTG, ZZ9000 cards in Zorro II and Zorro III) as a demand-class kernel module for the 68040/68060 module kernel kernel-k46-m (kabi k46.1.2): /etc/conf/mod.d/z3660rtg, /dev/zz9000 and /dev/zz9001 with their info nodes, /etc/display.d/z3660, zz9000 and zz9001, startx-rtg, the tools zz9k_probe, zz9k_monsw, rtg-kbdback and ztop, and the pages zz9000(7) and zz9k_probe(1M); needs the monsw module (monsw46).
DESC=The amix-z3660rtg framebuffer driver built as an amix-dlm kernel module for the 68040/68060 line (kabi k46.1.2): the Z3660's onboard RTG and MNT ZZ9000 cards, Zorro II and Zorro III.  Demand class, character major 49, loaded at the first open of one of its nodes; it depends on the monsw monitor-switch module (depend=monsw), without which kbootset refuses the generation at gate 3.  Two units: /dev/zz9000 (c 49 0) is the first board and /dev/zz9001 (c 49 1) the second; the Z3660 is always unit 0, a ZZ9000 beside it unit 1.  Both are 0660 root sys (the server and the monitor-switch tool run as root); their info nodes /dev/zz9000i and /dev/zz9001i (c 49 128 and 129, 0444) give the board's identity and sensors to any user.  Only the display registers are reachable; a ZZ9000's own pass-through is switched to the Amiga picture when X gives the display back and at the last close.  On a kernel that offers fb_register (kabi k46.1.6 and later) the framebuffer gets the fast cache class (noncacheable, not serialised); on the 1.1 kernels it keeps the default class.  For X the package ships the card files of display.d(4): /etc/display.d/z3660 (server /opt/amix/X11R6/bin/Xzz9000, modes 1024x768 to 1920x1080 at depth 16) and /etc/display.d/zz9000 and zz9001 (the same server, modes 1024x768 to 1920x800 at depth 16, 1920x1080 too on a Zorro III card, no monitor switch; zz9001 is a ZZ9000 beside a Z3660, unit 1, and needs x11r63 6.3-10 or later).  Each file's probe line runs /opt/amix/bin/zz9k_probe, which reads the board identity from the info nodes, so with amix-base 1.0-35 or later the automatic card choice picks the right file; an older base ignores the line and takes the first card whose node opens, z3660 first, so there set card zz9000 (or card zz9001 beside a Z3660) in /etc/display.  It also ships /opt/amix/bin/zz9k_monsw (the monitor-switch tool the z3660 file names), /opt/amix/bin/rtg-kbdback (gives the console its keyboard back after a server that ended on its own), /opt/amix/bin/ztop (the board's temperatures, voltages and CPU clock on a terminal) with its manual page, the page zz9000(7), and /opt/amix/bin/startx-rtg, the 1.1 launcher.  The same readings in an X window are the xztop package.  Parameters: blit, fixed (also try the Z3660 RTG at its fixed base, which a Z3660 running its emulated 68030 needs, when the AutoConfig list holds a Z3660 identity), kvfb (MiB of the framebuffer the kernel maps when the board lies above the identity map) and maxarea, in /etc/conf/modreg.d/z3660rtg, which holds the package's defaults (none).  The package writes no boot store; after the install apkg runs kbootset build and commit (or prints the command when bootset=manual).  Tested in emulation (Z3660 RTG and a ZZ9000 in Zorro II), not on a real ZZ9000.  MIT; links the stock console font object.
